WEBVTT

00:00:04.208 --> 00:00:06.688
That one there is Veritaserum.

00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:08.995
It's a truth-telling serum.

00:00:09.039 --> 00:00:11.868
And that would be Polyjuice
Potion.

00:00:15.306 --> 00:00:17.090
It's terribly tricky to make.

00:00:17.134 --> 00:00:18.831
And this is Amortentia,

00:00:18.875 --> 00:00:22.791
the most powerful
love potion in the world.

00:00:22.835 --> 00:00:24.924
It's rumored to smell
differently to each person

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:26.621
according to what attracts them.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.277
For example, I smell

00:00:30.321 --> 00:00:33.019
freshly mown grass,
and new parchment,

00:00:33.063 --> 00:00:37.328
and spearmint toothpaste.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:42.246
SLUGHORN:
Now, Amortentia doesn't
create actual love.

00:00:42.289 --> 00:00:43.900
That would be impossible.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:47.773
But it does cause a powerful
infatuation or obsession.

00:00:47.816 --> 00:00:49.949
And for that reason,

00:00:49.993 --> 00:00:53.910
it is probably the most
dangerous potion in this room.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.912
[♪♪♪]

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:03.484
Sir? You haven't told us
what's in that one.

00:01:03.528 --> 00:01:05.704
Oh, yes.

00:01:05.747 --> 00:01:08.402
What you see before you,
ladies and gentlemen

00:01:08.446 --> 00:01:10.970
is a curious little potion

00:01:11.014 --> 00:01:14.147
known as Felix Felicis.

00:01:14.191 --> 00:01:16.584
But it is more commonly
referred to as--

00:01:16.628 --> 00:01:17.846
Liquid luck.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:22.286
Yes, Miss Granger.
Liquid luck.

00:01:22.329 --> 00:01:23.591
Desperately tricky to make,

00:01:23.635 --> 00:01:26.159
disastrous should you
get it wrong.

00:01:26.203 --> 00:01:27.769
One sip and you will find

00:01:27.813 --> 00:01:30.816
that all of your
endeavors succeed.

00:01:33.253 --> 00:01:36.604
At least until
the effects wear off.

00:01:36.648 --> 00:01:40.608
So this is what I offer
each of you today.

00:01:40.652 --> 00:01:42.959
One tiny vial
of liquid luck

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.265
to the student who,
in the hour that remains,

00:01:45.309 --> 00:01:47.615
manages to brew
an acceptable Draught

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:50.314
of Living Death,

00:01:50.357 --> 00:01:53.665
the recipes for which can be
found on page 10 of your books.

00:01:53.708 --> 00:01:55.667
I should point out, however,

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.669
only once did a student manage
to brew a potion

00:01:57.712 --> 00:02:00.280
of sufficient quality to claim
this prize.

00:02:01.716 --> 00:02:04.632
Nevertheless,
good luck to you all.

00:02:04.676 --> 00:02:07.026
Let the brewing commence.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:09.072
[♪♪♪]

00:02:42.105 --> 00:02:44.759
How did you do that?

00:02:44.803 --> 00:02:46.979
You crush it. Don't cut it.

00:02:47.023 --> 00:02:49.677
No. The instructions
specifically say to cut.

00:02:49.721 --> 00:02:51.679
No, really.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:32.242
Merlin's beard.
It is perfect.

00:03:33.765 --> 00:03:37.029
So perfect I daresay
one drop would kill us all.

00:03:40.163 --> 00:03:42.904
So here we are, then,
as promised.

00:03:42.948 --> 00:03:45.559
One vial of Felix Felicis.

00:03:45.603 --> 00:03:48.127
Congratulations.

00:03:48.171 --> 00:03:50.608
Use it well.

00:04:11.498 --> 00:04:13.152
[KNOCKING]

00:04:18.288 --> 00:04:21.378
DUMBLEDORE:
Ah, Harry, you got my message.
Come in.

00:04:22.857 --> 00:04:24.120
How are you?

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:26.252
I'm fine, sir.

00:04:26.296 --> 00:04:27.601
Enjoying your classes?

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.519
I know Professor Slughorn
is most impressed with you.

00:04:32.563 --> 00:04:34.869
I think he overestimates
my abilities, sir.

00:04:34.913 --> 00:04:36.697
Oh, do you?

00:04:36.741 --> 00:04:38.134
Definitely.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.440
[DUMBLEDORE CHUCKLES]

00:04:40.484 --> 00:04:43.356
What about your activities
outside the classroom?

00:04:44.401 --> 00:04:46.403
Sir?Well, I notice you spend

00:04:46.446 --> 00:04:49.449
a great deal of time
with Miss Granger.

00:04:49.493 --> 00:04:50.798
I can't help wondering if--

00:04:50.842 --> 00:04:53.323
Oh, no, no. I mean,
she's brilliant,

00:04:53.366 --> 00:04:55.934
and we're friends, but, no.

00:04:55.977 --> 00:04:59.677
Forgive me. I was merely
being curious.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:02.114
But enough chitchat.

00:05:02.158 --> 00:05:06.249
You must be wondering
why I summoned you here tonight.

00:05:06.292 --> 00:05:09.904
The answer lies here.

00:05:09.948 --> 00:05:12.472
What you are looking
at are memories.

00:05:12.516 --> 00:05:16.433
In this case, pertaining
to one individual, Voldemort,

00:05:16.476 --> 00:05:19.087
or, as he was known then,
Tom Riddle.

00:05:22.047 --> 00:05:26.007
This vial contains
the most particular memory

00:05:26.051 --> 00:05:28.140
of the day I first met him.

00:05:29.533 --> 00:05:32.449
I'd like you to see it,
if you would.

00:05:43.068 --> 00:05:45.070
[♪♪♪]

